    "finalText": "Everything checks out. The URL Shortener API is complete and verified:\n\n**What was built** — a Rails 8.0.2 (exact version, pinned in Gemfile) API-only app on Ruby 3.4.3 with PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`:\n\n- `POST /links` — 201 with `{\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\": 0}`, URL stored unchanged; auto-generates unique 7-char codes; 409 on duplicate custom code (unique index + `RecordNotUnique` rescue); 422 for invalid/missing url (custom `UrlValidator` requiring absolute http/https with host), invalid codes (4–20 of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`), and malformed JSON\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 or 404 JSON error; `GET /r/{code}` — 302 with Location set, atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` increment; `GET /links` — `{\"items\", \"total\"}` in ascending creation order\n- `start.sh` — runs `bin/rails db:prepare` (verified it creates and migrates a fresh database) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup\n\n**Verified end-to-end**: every status path, redirect Location header, missing Content-Type handling, 4/20-char code boundaries, and a full restart cycle confirming data and click counts persist. Test rows were cleaned up afterward, so the database is empty for the graded run, and no server is left occupying port 8000."
